  Why tun2proxy is the Solution:

  ✅ Explicit HTTP Proxy Support

  From the README:
  - "HTTP proxy support (unauthenticated, basic and digest auth)"
  - Works with: --proxy "http://192.168.49.1:8000"

  ✅ Proper Implementation

  Looking at the code (src/http.rs), it correctly implements HTTP CONNECT:
  - Sends CONNECT hostname:port HTTP/1.1 for tunneling
  - Handles authentication (Basic/Digest)
  - Waits for 200 Connection established response
  - Then forwards raw traffic through the tunnel

  ✅ Android-Ready

  - Has build-android.sh script that builds native .so libraries
  - Provides JNI bindings via android.rs
  - Simple API:
  Tun2proxy.run(
      proxyUrl: "http://192.168.49.1:8000",
      tunFd: vpnInterface.getFd(),
      closeFdOnDrop: false,
      tunMtu: 1500,
      verbosity: 2,
      dnsStrategy: 0
  )

  ✅ Modern & Maintained

  - Written in Rust (fast, safe)
  - Cross-platform (Linux, Android, macOS, iOS, Windows)
  - Actively maintained
  - Supports IPv4/IPv6, UDP, DNS over TCP

  How to Integrate:

  1. Clone and build for Android:
  cd /home/jonathan/Desktop/pdanet-client
  git clone https://github.com/tun2proxy/tun2proxy.git
